title: Prompt that triggers an Xberg tool call
---
sequenceDiagram
  %% Source for 24-xberg-tool-call-flow.html. Edit this file, then run ./scripts/render-diagrams.py.
  %% Directives: docs in diagrams/README.md (Updating diagrams).
  %% @subtitle The user only writes a prompt; the chat app offers the xberg tools, the model decides to call extract, and LiteLLM runs the call and asks the model again in the same request
  %% @type frontend: APP
  %% @type cloud: TR
  %% @type security: PR EG
  %% @type external: OAI WEB
  %% @type database: OBS
  actor U as User
  participant APP as Chat app or agent<br/>Chat UI · IDE · SDK
  participant TR as Traefik<br/>TLS + edge limits
  participant LL as LiteLLM proxy<br/>auth · MCP gateway
  participant PR as Presidio<br/>PII masking
  participant OAI as OpenAI<br/>provider model
  participant XB as Xberg MCP<br/>xberg-sandbox
  participant EG as Egress guard<br/>xberg-dns + Squid
  participant WEB as Allowlisted website<br/>e.g. docs.xberg.io
  participant OBS as Telemetry<br/>spend · metrics · spans

  U->>APP: prompt: summarise https://docs.xberg.io/…
  Note over APP: the app, not the user, adds the xberg MCP tools (server_url litellm_proxy, require_approval never)
  APP->>TR: POST /v1/chat/completions: prompt + mcp tool
  TR->>LL: route by host
  Note over LL: authenticate the key; the key or team must be granted xberg
  LL->>PR: pre_call: mask PII in the prompt
  PR-->>LL: masked prompt
  LL->>XB: MCP tools/list
  XB-->>LL: tool definitions
  Note over LL: keep the four allowed_tools; in dev, BGE-M3 keeps the 3 that best match the prompt
  LL->>OAI: prompt + tool definitions
  Note over OAI: the model decides whether a tool is needed and writes its arguments from the prompt
  alt model answers directly
    OAI-->>LL: completion, no tool call
  else model requests the tool
    OAI-->>LL: tool_call: xberg-extract(uri)
    Note over LL: LiteLLM executes the call itself; the app never sees the tool_call
    LL->>XB: MCP tools/call extract
    XB->>XB: check the URL against the SSRF allowlist
    XB->>EG: resolve the host, HTTPS CONNECT :443
    alt host unlisted, private, or plain HTTP
      EG--xXB: NXDOMAIN or 403 denied
      XB--xLL: tool error, sent to the model as the result
    else host allowlisted
      EG->>WEB: TLS tunnel to the host
      WEB-->>XB: document through the tunnel
      XB-->>LL: extracted text
      LL->>LL: post_mcp_call: mask injection phrases
      Note over LL: dev: a trusted caller's extraction is also indexed in the background (Xberg auto-indexing)
    end
    LL->>OAI: follow-up: prompt + tool call + tool result
    OAI-->>LL: final answer
  end
  LL->>PR: post_call: mask PII in the answer
  PR-->>LL: masked answer
  LL-)OBS: spend logs, metrics, content-free spans for model and tool calls
  LL-->>TR: response with MCP tool metadata
  TR-->>APP: response
  APP-->>U: answer
